<figure class="cache-figure" data-retry-expansion>
 <p class="figure-title">Retries at two layers multiply the work</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>Application attempts <select data-outer aria-label="Application attempts"><option>1</option><option>2</option><option selected>3</option></select></label><label>Loader attempts per call <select data-inner aria-label="Loader attempts"><option>1</option><option>2</option><option selected>3</option></select></label></div>
 <div class="retry-root">One user request</div><div class="retry-tree" data-tree></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>Every attempt fails, so every permitted retry runs. Three attempts means one initial attempt and two retries. The leaves are source operations, not simultaneous jobs. Backoff and jitter can separate their start times; they do not reduce this worst-case count.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import {retryExpansion} from '../../lib/caching/failures.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-retry-expansion]').forEach(root=>{const outer=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-outer]')!,inner=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-inner]')!;const render=()=>{const s=retryExpansion(+outer.value,+inner.value);root.querySelector('[data-tree]')!.replaceChildren(...s.branches.map((branch,i)=>{const group=document.createElement('div');const label=document.createElement('strong');label.textContent=`App attempt ${i+1}`;group.append(label);for(const leaf of branch){const item=document.createElement('span');item.textContent=`Source ${leaf.outer}.${leaf.inner}`;group.append(item);}return group;}));root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=`${s.outer} × ${s.inner} = ${s.leaves} source attempts for one user request. ${s.outer>1&&s.inner>1?'Retrying independently at both layers amplifies the load.':'Only one layer retries, or neither does.'}`;};outer.onchange=inner.onchange=render;render();});
</script>
